{
  "requirement": "The authoring harness MUST use Rig and support Bedrock and Ollama. Users MUST be\nable to select a backend and model through configuration without changing the\nassessment tools, prompt, or evidence format.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the requirement is met. Rig is used for both backends. Backend and model come from configuration. The prompt, tools and evidence format do not depend on the backend. I did not read the config parser in `src/config`; I relied on the other requirements that cover configuration for how a backend and model are selected.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `RigProvider::connect` (`src/authoring/providers.rs:105-134`) is marked `{impl}`. It matches on `BackendConfig` and builds a Rig `DynModel<Completion>`:\n  - Bedrock uses `rig_bedrock::client::BedrockRuntime` over the AWS SDK client.\n  - Ollama uses `rig_core::providers::ollama::OllamaConfig`.\n  - Both use `config.model` as the model name, so the model comes from configuration.\n- `configured_record` (`src/authoring/mod.rs:352-388`) is marked `{impl}`. It records the backend and model from the resolved config. It then calls `RigProvider::connect(&config.backend)` and hands the provider to the shared `assess` function. Source preparation and the assessment loop do not depend on the backend.\n- The `CompletionProvider::complete` trait method and `RigProvider::complete` are marked `{impl}`. The trait is the one abstraction over both backends, so the tools, prompt and evidence path are shared.\n- `normalize_bedrock_client_calls` is marked `{impl}`. It adapts Bedrock's typed `tool_use` blocks into Rig client tool calls. It keeps the native item for replay and reports malformed calls (missing `toolUseId`, missing `name`, or non-object `input`).\n- Other code in `providers.rs`, such as SDK loader setup, option mapping, backoff and credentials, is marked `{impl}` for the requirements that specify it. I found no unmarked behaviour that belongs to this requirement. `struct RigProvider` carries only a `{cite}`, which is harmless because the `{impl}` markers sit on the functions that do the work.\n\n**Tests**\n- `both_adapters_send_the_same_prompt_and_tools_with_default_connections` (`tests/authoring_cli.rs:1541`) runs Ollama and Bedrock through the CLI against mock servers, each selected only by config. It asserts that the prompt and the six tool definitions are identical across the two backends. That is the \"without changing tools or prompt\" obligation.\n- `bedrock_cli_uses_selected_profile_region_and_converse_tools` (`tests/authoring_cli.rs:1210`) covers Bedrock end to end with both untyped and typed tool-use. It checks the Converse endpoint and the model in the path, profile and region signing, options mapping, and tool schemas. It also checks that the evidence file is produced and that usage records backend `bedrock` and the configured model.\n- `authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file` (`tests/authoring_cli.rs:434`) selects Ollama and a model purely through configuration and checks that `workspace-model` reaches the request body and the usage record.\n- The unit tests in `providers.rs` cover tool-call normalization:\n  - `typed_client_calls_preserve_order_and_native_history` covers ordering, hosted and unknown `toolUse` types, idempotence, and preservation of origin and raw data.\n  - `malformed_typed_client_calls_are_reported` covers three failure cases.\n- `tests/live_bedrock.rs` adds an opt-in live Bedrock test that is skipped under CI.\n\nBoth required backends, configuration-driven selection, invariance of tools and prompt, and the failure cases of the Bedrock adapter are all exercised. I found no gaps and no FIXME markers.",
